<Base title="The practical details." description="Terms for using Howloop’s educational calculators, guides and public banking product information."><header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / terms</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">HOWLOOP · THE DETAILS</span><h1 style="max-width:900px">The practical details.</h1></header><article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><p class="hl-page-meta">Updated 18 September 2026</p><h2>Educational use</h2><p>Howloop provides general educational tools and information. It does not provide personal financial advice, credit assistance, legal advice or tax advice. A result is not a recommendation, a forecast, a quote, loan approval or an offer from a financial institution.</p><h2>Assumptions and accuracy</h2><p>Calculator results depend on the values you enter and the stated assumptions. Real outcomes may differ because of changing rates, dates, fees, rounding, tax, product conditions or your circumstances. Read the relevant <a href="/methodology">calculation method</a> and check current information with the provider before relying on an estimate.</p><h2>Product information</h2><p>The bank directory uses dated public data snapshots. Coverage is incomplete and some feeds may be unavailable. Bank names and marks belong to their respective owners; inclusion does not establish an endorsement, partnership or product ranking.</p><h2>Your use of the site</h2><p>Use the site lawfully. Do not interfere with availability, attempt unauthorised access or misrepresent the source of our content. You can use calculator results for your own planning and may link to the site. Third-party material remains subject to its owner’s rights.</p><h2>Availability and responsibility</h2><p>We aim to make the tools useful but cannot guarantee uninterrupted access or that every source remains current. Nothing in these terms is intended to exclude rights or remedies that cannot lawfully be excluded. For decisions requiring advice about your circumstances, speak with an appropriately qualified professional.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Send questions and correction reports to <a href="mailto:hello@howloop.how">hello@howloop.how</a>. Our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> explains how calculator inputs and correspondence are handled.</p></article></Base>
